source is publicly readable is not a license to use it. Except for the
limited permissions in sections 1 and 2, and except for the third-party
material in section 4, all rights in the original code and original assets
are reserved by the copyright holder.

1. PERMITTED — PLAYING OFFICIAL BUILDS

   You may download, install and run an official Harbourlife build published
   by the copyright holder on this repository's GitHub Releases page, for
   personal, non-commercial play and testing, on hardware you control.

2. PERMITTED — READING AND LOCAL EVALUATION OF SOURCE

   You may view and study the source in this repository, and compile it
   locally for the sole purpose of evaluating it. You may not distribute the
   source, any modified form of it, or any build produced from it.

3. RESERVED — NOT PERMITTED WITHOUT PRIOR WRITTEN PERMISSION

   All of the following are reserved to the copyright holder:

   a. Redistributing, mirroring, re-uploading, reselling, renting, lending or
      sublicensing the original code, the original assets, or any build.
   b. Creating or publishing derivative works, ports, modifications or forks,
      in whole or in part, on any platform.
   c. Any commercial use, including use inside a commercial product, service,
      advertisement, paid stream, paid course or paid asset pack.
   d. Using the original code or original assets as training data, or
      including them in a corpus or dataset for machine learning.
   e. Removing, obscuring or altering this notice, the in-game attribution,
      or the notices in PLAY_PERMISSION.md and the licenses/ directory.

   Nothing in this section limits rights you have under applicable law that
   cannot be excluded by contract, or under GitHub's Terms of Service.

